 role  of spectator in certain situations  aren't you  yeah but that comes with being a keeper  i'm not unhappy with my situation  i became a keeper because i wanted to  i know what my role is and what  strengths will help the team  that's all i can do a keeper rarely wins  a match the best of keeper can do is  keep his team in the game  what does nuremberg have to do to stay  in the running win  what does nuremberg have to do to win  maybe we have to try at the decisive  moments to play with efficiency  aggressiveness and drive  we absolutely have to win two matches  and if we do i'm certain we'll end up in  the end of season playoffs  we'll do what we have to do to stay in  the league  and i don't care if braunschweig hamburg  stuttgart or some other team ends up  behind us  but it's important for us to do our  homework and to win our matches and then  we won't have to depend on some team  losing and us winning in the final round  i think it's important for us to work  everything out in advance so we can take  action  do you have any kind of sympathy for  your competitors  nobody has any sympathy for us why  should they this is a sport not a  chronic disease if it were a disease i  could sympathize  but this is a matter of leaving two or  if all goes well three teams behind you  that's the objective  it's a sporting endeavor not one that  affects health or lifestyle  except for the way it affects the fans  but that's something else  this is a sport  a competition  you
 

